  2958	- Decided (the general rule under all seven: two questions are one when the same outcome settles both; they are kept apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on each separately):
  2959	  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, "A"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. A not-yet-signed deal is a yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart); whether it merges into the plan's amount question follows the same bet-separately test, judged per case in the gold (the Ohio lease guarantee against the cloud-customer total in v38). Narrows the standard §4 "another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.
  2960	  2. **One event, several deadlines** (H2, "A"): while the earlier-deadline question is open, a later deadline is its evidence, not a new question; when the earlier one falls due unresolved and the matter is still live, the system opens the next-deadline successor with the merged evidence, without waiting for a new article (new work for pull mode, D14, D54).
  2961	  3. **One product generation, several milestones** (H3, "A"): one question per generation, asked at the step that brings revenue (shipments begin); sampling and launch are its evidence; only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's phase-3 data and its approval) are separate questions.
  2962	  4. **A company's own quantity by fiscal and by calendar year** (H4, "A"): only the fiscal year opens (PRD 06 ladder rule 5); a calendar-year estimate is evidence to the fiscal question, weighed lower when the years differ much.
  2963	  5. **A model-written period start** (H5, "A"): for event and policy questions it no longer blocks a merge; object, event and due day are still checked.
  2964	  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, "A， A"): a question opens only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise the statement is evidence. Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C ("a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition").
  2965	  7. **The same statement carried by several outlets** (H7, "A"): code treats pieces with the same original speaker, original day and figures as one; the judge sees it once with the outlet count; every piece is still stored. Changes D204's "both shown to the judge" for this case; the risk put to him with the question (a qualification such as "excluding China sales" hidden; D204's 8 of 40 wrong merges) is measured on the G3 gold before it is switched on, as is the accuracy of the original-speaker and original-day fields it relies on.
  2966	- Next, in this order: the signed standard page (§3 class C, §4 "same question, succession or another question") carries these rules, then a read-only Codex drift review; then the plan's step 1 (structured census, the fixed-extraction replay harness, gold G1–G3, the September holdout week on Alex's go).

