docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-9.log:1942:7. **H5’s stated change does not cover every use of the start date.** [Plan lines 96 and 154](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:96) propose removing the start date from conflict checking. It also enters the automatic identity key ([identity.py lines 18–32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:18)), list construction ([matching.py lines 122–144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:122)), and succession eligibility ([jev_matching.py lines 95–101](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:95)). The proposed change may fix the two observed cases, but the plan has not yet shown it removes the counted class or preserves the other paths.
