docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-9.log:1960:5. **Serious — H2’s key future transition is not exercised by the stated replay.** [Plan lines 94 and 176]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:94) propose opening a later question when the earlier deadline expires. The stored Kyber example’s earlier deadline is December 31, 2027, while the sealed replay ends in August 2026. The [planned measurements]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:142) do not state a check that advances through that expiry. A replay could pass while the deferred successor never opens.
docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-9.log:1966:The ACP “guarantee and financing” sentence is in both the [signed standard, line 318]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318) and the [collision prompt]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1). The revised plan no longer claims it caused the split or that the two standard sentences necessarily conflict. H1–H5 now name their relevant boundaries as choices; H7’s lean retains D204’s two records. The census totals match the recorded outputs, but its verdict categories remain provisional because the [script parses reason text]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:18). I did not independently verify every archived verdict, quotation or cost estimate.
docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-9.log:1998:The central source checks support several corrections already made. The guarantee/financing sentence is in both the [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318) and the [collision prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1); its causing the ACP split remains unproven, as the plan now says. H1–H7 identify their principal changes as choices, and H7’s lean agrees with [D204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2609). The displayed census totals match the saved outputs, but verdict classes still depend on reason-text parsing ([census script line 25](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:25)). I did not independently verify every archived verdict, quote, estimate, or factual claim.
