docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-9.log:3763:docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/review-1.txt:13:5. **H1, H3 and the general rule add boundaries that the standard does not settle.** [Plan lines 80–82 and 86–88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:80) add “when uncertain, merge,” “one plan, one question,” and “one product generation, one question.” The signed standard does say one outcome can settle two questions ([line 316](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:316)), so that part is correctly attributed. It also requires separation where answers can move apart ([line 274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:274)), and [D236](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2871) permits a launch **or** shipment question; it does not decide that all milestones are one question. D243’s caution about noisy extraction is not a decision to merge uncertain questions ([standard lines 153–156](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:153)). The v38 ledger’s `v11` launch and `v17` shipment are a concrete case requiring that distinction.
